<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siraces</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Siraci</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siraces were a Sarmatian people of the plains of the Kuban river, north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, from about the fourth century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> records that they were ruled by kings and could field tens of thousands of horsemen. Their king Zorsines supported the deposed Bosporan king Mithridates in 49 CE and was defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aorsi">Aorsi</a>, as described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>.</p></div>
